{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998315-gameline-as-police-force-prescinct","id":998315,"title":"Gameline As: Police Force/Prescinct","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-04T10:59:48-07:00","id":998315,"title":"Gameline As: Police Force/Prescinct","content":"This edition of Gameline As: How would each of the supernaturals work as the members/controllers of a police force, and by which I mean, one primarily charged with the usual police enforcement work (focused on Mortals, not Supernaturals - though obviously some policing of the shadows is probably necessary).<br /> <br /> Werewolves and Sin-Eaters probably have it easy, but Vampires, Mummies, and Prometheans probably are a bit harder to pull off. Either way - discuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:11:04-07:00","id":998323,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the nosferatu as the 'bad' cop and the daeva as the 'good' cop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:19:40-07:00","id":998326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998315-gameline-as-police-force-prescinct?p=998323#post998323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of the nosferatu as the 'bad' cop and the daeva as the 'good' cop.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Mekhet as the basement/lab dwelling CSI tech?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:22:17-07:00","id":998327,"title":"","content":"There's a vampire detective in one of the clanbooks, the Dead Lieutenant. Pretty interesting section from that book, I recall.<br /> <br /> Werewolves have the Lodge of the Shield for support. From there I guess it would really depend on how good they want to be. Blood tracking, enhanced senses, and the Gifts would allow them to be basically super cops, though follow-through with convictions might be hard if the pack didn't extend to the judiciary. Of course there's always the alternative to courtroom justice in the form of tooth and claw. Obviously clearing out all crime would lead to other issues, which wouldn't necessarily be a good thing. I could see packs getting gung-ho about the idea until they realized what was filling that vacuum. In the end they would either have to ease off and try to narrow things down to important cases, or just don the purple gloves and bull through. The Pack has a similar idea throughout the first chapter with the fire department Pack.<br /> <br /> I always wanted to do a vampire and werewolf buddy cop game.<br /> <br /> Hunter would be very interesting, sort of like the Shield, balancing illegalities with the necessity of their vigil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:24:30-07:00","id":998330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998315-gameline-as-police-force-prescinct?p=998327#post998327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a vampire detective in one of the clanbooks, the Dead Lieutenant. Pretty interesting section from that book, I recall.<br /> <br /> Werewolves have the Lodge of the Shield for support. From there I guess it would really depend on how good they want to be. Blood tracking, enhanced senses, and the Gifts would allow them to be basically super cops, though follow-through with convictions might be hard if the pack didn't extend to the judiciary. Of course there's always the alternative to courtroom justice in the form of tooth and claw. Obviously clearing out all crime would lead to other issues, which wouldn't necessarily be a good thing. I could see packs getting gung-ho about the idea until they realized what was filling that vacuum. In the end they would either have to ease off and try to narrow things down to important cases, or just don the purple gloves and bull through. The Pack has a similar idea throughout the first chapter with the fire department Pack.<br /> <br /> I always wanted to do a vampire and werewolf buddy cop game.<br /> <br /> Hunter would be very interesting, sort of like the Shield, balancing illegalities with the necessity of their vigil.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you think would be their outlook on K-9 officers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:35:07-07:00","id":998340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998315-gameline-as-police-force-prescinct?p=998330#post998330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think would be their outlook on K-9 officers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not noteworthy. I mean, some people are going to be closer to animals than others but werewolves don't have that tendency by dint of being Uratha. I suppose if one was going to be a K-9 officer, they might want to pick up the Beast Talker Gift. Really, the senses of a werewolf can be better than those of a K-9, especially with the added ability to think things through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:24:22-07:00","id":998373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998315-gameline-as-police-force-prescinct?p=998340#post998340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not noteworthy. I mean, some people are going to be closer to animals than others but werewolves don't have that tendency by dint of being Uratha. I suppose if one was going to be a K-9 officer, they might want to pick up the Beast Talker Gift. Really, the senses of a werewolf can be better than those of a K-9, especially with the added ability to think things through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Na, the Pack says they can get pretty close to wolves. Dogs are just a domesticated sort of wolf, so I imagine there'd be some ease of relations there. But in practical terms, yes the werewolves would probably be able to do that work just fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:37:01-07:00","id":998387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998315-gameline-as-police-force-prescinct?p=998373#post998373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Na, the Pack says they can get pretty close to wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it does not say all Uratha are naturally close to wolves. Like I said, it's going to depend on the individual, and just because they're an Uratha doesn't mean they're an animal person or want to be a K-9 officer. That's more of an Apocalypse Garou thing, though offhand I think they wouldn't like the police aspect.<br /> <br /> Then there's the 'Caging the Wolves' section which warns against things like bringing a wolf on a Siskur-Dah then trying to cage them. A K-9 officer can't let their dog run free, especially after having tasted the blood of others, and being leashed and caged, then let out solely to bring things down, is going to create a vicious animal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:39:56-07:00","id":998389,"title":"","content":"I'm actually a little enamoured with the aesthetics of law enforcement officials abusing their office for ambitious ends. I have the FBI to thank for the example, lately.<br /> <br /> The discretionary power of a police chief to redirect resources, waive or bring charges, and otherwise exercise authority over deciding where the blinding light of authority is aimed is a really tempting prize for any supernatural. Lately, I've been thinking of the Silver Ladder subverting such institutions.<br /> <br /> When the chief of police sincerely believes in fighting the good fight, and they've got actual miracle workers behind the scenes, one can only imagine a city tends to improve under their auspice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:58:23-07:00","id":998400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998315-gameline-as-police-force-prescinct?p=998389#post998389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually a little enamoured with the aesthetics of law enforcement officials abusing their office for ambitious ends. I have the FBI to thank for the example, lately.<br /> <br /> The discretionary power of a police chief to redirect resources, waive or bring charges, and otherwise exercise authority over deciding where the blinding light of authority is aimed is a really tempting prize for any supernatural. Lately, I've been thinking of the Silver Ladder subverting such institutions.<br /> <br /> When the chief of police sincerely believes in fighting the good fight, and they've got actual miracle workers behind the scenes, one can only imagine a city tends to improve under their auspice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Details, details, if you would?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T15:54:31-07:00","id":998481,"title":"","content":"Sure. Any part in particular you want details on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T18:05:50-07:00","id":998529,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that Sin Eaters would have it harder than you'd expect as police officers. A lot of evidence would work as an anchor for a ghost, as would the body, meaning any Bound working with the bodies or the evidence lockers would have a <i>ton</i> of unfinished business calling for them to work on. Plus, even if they'd make the ghost's business be finished, they'd not be able to take advantage of the resulting items to make charms - it'd be locked away in the evidence lockers. On the other hand, they'd have a pretty ready supply of plasm for helping ghosts, and they'd have a wealth of powers that would help them forensically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T10:17:21-08:00","id":1000865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998315-gameline-as-police-force-prescinct?p=998481#post998481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. Any part in particular you want details on?</div> </div> </div> </div>The complications you were envisioning. And how you'd envision such groups abusing their authority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T10:19:03-08:00","id":1000867,"title":"","content":"Also, does anyone have any ideas on how a Throng would work as a Police force? Given Roles and the changes to Disquiet and Wasteland, it is more viable than in 1E, but how would that work? I'd assume they'd have to be restricted to a smaller locale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T15:04:14-08:00","id":1001008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998315-gameline-as-police-force-prescinct?p=1000865#post1000865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The complications you were envisioning. And how you'd envision such groups abusing their authority.</div> </div> </div> </div>How I envision them abusing their authority is a laundry list, really. In theory, the noble cause of the Ladder would mean that police resources would be turned against the Seers and their witting and unwitting servants. This means putting police officers on investigations into things that weaken the Ladder's works and taking them off of things that strengthen it. For example, if a group of Seer minions are stockpiling guns and ammo, you can bet the Ladder is throwing police at them non-stop. On the other hand, Arrow gun runners might just be given a pass on their less-than-legal moving of firearms, so long as they put them to use serving the Ladder's purposes. If there's a corrupt politician working for the Seers, have their accounts investigated. If they work for you, have the police delay long enough for you to wipe out the evidence.<br /> <br /> But that's the pure ideals. In practice, the Ladder would probably abuse the hell out of this for personal goals as much as idealistic ones. Have the police overlook your purchases of psychotropic drugs for your cult. If someone dies in the pursuit of a Mystery (a terrible accident, to be sure, and not at all a result of your gross negligence), get it ruled a death by misadventure. Hell, get a speeding ticket thrown out because you were chasing a werewolf down the I-80.<br /> <br /> The leeway granted police is fairly substantial.<br /> <br /> The only problem is when competing factions start warring for control. That can get messy.<br /> <br /> It's actually a surprisingly simple thing for a Mage to ruin a mortal's career. When the mandatory police physical shows up, cast a spell to put cocaine in their blood stream and stick a kilo of Colombian marching powder in their sock drawer. The rest of the investigation doesn't need to hold up or turn up anything because the initial evidence is so damning and the subsequent evidence so confirming that no-one will question anything else.<br /> <br /> But... Once you do that, the door is open. Anyone else can do the exact same thing to your candidate. A Seer drugs your candidate and puts forward a fascist thug of a police chief as a replacement. Luckily, fascists tend to have their vices so you can probably get them knocked out of their job pretty easily just by following them around enough. Put the video on Youtube and send it to a few news channels and there is not a hope in hell of the enemy stopping it; by the time they even know about it, the damage is likely done.<br /> <br /> After that, though, it's your turn to put forth a candidate and suddenly you're both competing to put someone in power. Once that happens, there's only three possible outcomes:<br /> <br /> 1. Someone blinks, loses their nerve, and surrenders the contest.<br /> 2. Negotiation. Each party finds a candidate the other accepts and an accord is made; either one party controls the institution in exchange for an oath to the other not to use it on them (and a guarantee of resources, like grimoires, tass, etc.), or both find someone they can live with, step aside, and let mortal politics be untouched. That really means, though, that each just has to be more circumspect in their influence.<br /> 3. War. The cabals engage in direct combat. This is <i>not</i> going to be a pretty affair but it will be decisive, because the losers are either dead or have fled the coop. In the meantime, the organization is left to its own devices or radically destabilized by feuding sorcerers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T00:07:44-08:00","id":1001231,"title":"","content":"Yeah, mages in police really do look scarily hyper-competent. They're basically the Conspiracy splat (shudder)<br /> <br /> On the other hand, they're also the Investigator splat - Moros make the best forensics specialist, Mastigos the best interrogator, and such. Acanthus and Thyrsus would also make themselves useful in a CSI team. Obrimos I can't quite pin down as police... Prime to filter out lies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T02:53:44-08:00","id":1001279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998315-gameline-as-police-force-prescinct?p=1001231#post1001231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, mages in police really do look scarily hyper-competent. They're basically the Conspiracy splat (shudder)<br /> <br /> On the other hand, they're also the Investigator splat - Moros make the best forensics specialist, Mastigos the best interrogator, and such. Acanthus and Thyrsus would also make themselves useful in a CSI team. Obrimos I can't quite pin down as police... Prime to filter out lies?</div> </div> </div> </div>SWAT team?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T03:45:45-08:00","id":1001290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998315-gameline-as-police-force-prescinct?p=1001279#post1001279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SWAT team?</div> </div> </div> </div>I second that.<br /> <br /> On another note, changelings have even greater variety in police roles based on kith alone. The Cleareyes, Slewfoot, and Riddleseeker could work for detective-type characters, and I can see Antiquarians and Firehearts as competent CSIs.<br /> <br /> The Skogsra is ideal for someone who works with K9 units. As is my homebrewed <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1elqCKhNJweqnLuUy8Rbh2PiZSsnccnXQWrNy8cPf5o4/mobilebasic\" target=\"_blank\">Wildling</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 11-10-2016, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T07:39:01-08:00","id":1001350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998315-gameline-as-police-force-prescinct?p=1001290#post1001290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I second that.<br /> <br /> On another note, changelings have even greater variety in police roles based on kith alone. The Cleareyes, Slewfoot, and Riddleseeker could work for detective-type characters, and I can see Antiquarians and Firehearts as competent CSIs.<br /> <br /> The Skogsra is ideal for someone who works with K9 units. As is my homebrewed <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1elqCKhNJweqnLuUy8Rbh2PiZSsnccnXQWrNy8cPf5o4/mobilebasic\" target=\"_blank\">Wildling</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Court of the Shield or Badge, maybe? Or just an Entitlement?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T09:06:15-08:00","id":1001374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998315-gameline-as-police-force-prescinct?p=1001008#post1001008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How I envision them abusing their authority is a laundry list, really. In theory, the noble cause of the Ladder would mean that police resources would be turned against the Seers and their witting and unwitting servants. This means putting police officers on investigations into things that weaken the Ladder's works and taking them off of things that strengthen it. For example, if a group of Seer minions are stockpiling guns and ammo, you can bet the Ladder is throwing police at them non-stop. On the other hand, Arrow gun runners might just be given a pass on their less-than-legal moving of firearms, so long as they put them to use serving the Ladder's purposes. If there's a corrupt politician working for the Seers, have their accounts investigated. If they work for you, have the police delay long enough for you to wipe out the evidence.<br /> <br /> But that's the pure ideals. In practice, the Ladder would probably abuse the hell out of this for personal goals as much as idealistic ones. Have the police overlook your purchases of psychotropic drugs for your cult. If someone dies in the pursuit of a Mystery (a terrible accident, to be sure, and not at all a result of your gross negligence), get it ruled a death by misadventure. Hell, get a speeding ticket thrown out because you were chasing a werewolf down the I-80.<br /> <br /> The leeway granted police is fairly substantial.<br /> <br /> The only problem is when competing factions start warring for control. That can get messy.<br /> <br /> It's actually a surprisingly simple thing for a Mage to ruin a mortal's career. When the mandatory police physical shows up, cast a spell to put cocaine in their blood stream and stick a kilo of Colombian marching powder in their sock drawer. The rest of the investigation doesn't need to hold up or turn up anything because the initial evidence is so damning and the subsequent evidence so confirming that no-one will question anything else.<br /> <br /> But... Once you do that, the door is open. Anyone else can do the exact same thing to your candidate. A Seer drugs your candidate and puts forward a fascist thug of a police chief as a replacement. Luckily, fascists tend to have their vices so you can probably get them knocked out of their job pretty easily just by following them around enough. Put the video on Youtube and send it to a few news channels and there is not a hope in hell of the enemy stopping it; by the time they even know about it, the damage is likely done.<br /> <br /> After that, though, it's your turn to put forth a candidate and suddenly you're both competing to put someone in power. Once that happens, there's only three possible outcomes:<br /> <br /> 1. Someone blinks, loses their nerve, and surrenders the contest.<br /> 2. Negotiation. Each party finds a candidate the other accepts and an accord is made; either one party controls the institution in exchange for an oath to the other not to use it on them (and a guarantee of resources, like grimoires, tass, etc.), or both find someone they can live with, step aside, and let mortal politics be untouched. That really means, though, that each just has to be more circumspect in their influence.<br /> 3. War. The cabals engage in direct combat. This is <i>not</i> going to be a pretty affair but it will be decisive, because the losers are either dead or have fled the coop. In the meantime, the organization is left to its own devices or radically destabilized by feuding sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have very entertaining image of a character that was a victim of this. Say, a police officer who got on a tail of Arrow Gun-Runner and after multiple attempts to throw her off, she was finally disposed of using the method your described. Which then makes her motivated to get deep into the things, and leads into her Awakening.<br /> Awkwardness ensues when she is introduced into the society and, uh, figures out what ruined her life. &quot;...but it lead into your Awakening and thus you probably should thank us, no? See, it all worked out.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T12:12:16-08:00","id":1001424,"title":"","content":"And that, gentlemen, is how I became a Banisher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T23:46:09-08:00","id":1001649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998315-gameline-as-police-force-prescinct?p=1001231#post1001231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, mages in police really do look scarily hyper-competent. They're basically the Conspiracy splat (shudder)<br /> <br /> On the other hand, they're also the Investigator splat - Moros make the best forensics specialist, Mastigos the best interrogator, and such. Acanthus and Thyrsus would also make themselves useful in a CSI team. Obrimos I can't quite pin down as police... Prime to filter out lies?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Let's do this:<br /> <br /> All Obrimos can hear radio waves without any apparati as well as allow their entire team to do so as well. All Obrimos can move with awesome efficiency and see in the dark perfectly.<br /> Most Obrimos can become invisible and speak over radio waves without actually having a radio, they can ensure favorable weather for themselves and bad weather for enemies as well as zoom in like with a scope, but better in every way.<br /> Some Obrimos can control the momentum and velocity of things (like bullets).<br /> <br /> All Obrimos can dispel existing magic and see through any lies. They can see Mana, Hallows and magical proficiency and detect Nodes, Hallows, Avernian Gateways, Verges and even stranger things.<br /> Most Obrimos can cloak their own, or other people's Nimbus, write invisible messages in the magical language of &quot;cannot lie ever&quot; as well as shield themselves from hostile magic and make any truths they state be believed by any who hear them.<br /> Some Obrimos can move Mana around, cleanse the effects of Focused Revelation, make safe areas of &quot;THIS IS MAGIC&quot;, punch (or shoot) spirits, ghosts and angels, move ley lines and make Sleepers into Sleepwalkers.<br /> <br /> So yes, Obrimos are both SWAT teams and the infininitely more terrifying:<br /> <br /> Legal teams.<br /> <br /> (Using Forces to manipulate surveillance records and Prime to be believed when they speak the truth while communicating with other mages in invisible High Speech.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}